    {
      "name": "8. Embassy SSO (preferred for mobile)",
      "description": "Single sign-on flow when FMS is embedded under the Embassy app.\n\n**Testing order (2 steps):**\n1. Run **'Exchange handoff for FMS token'** — paste the handoff token minted by the Embassy backend in the `{{handoff_token}}` variable, then run. On success, the FMS access token is auto-saved to `{{token}}`.\n2. Run **'Verify auth via /api/demo'** — confirms the access token works.\n\nAfter step 1, every other request in this collection authenticates automatically (collection-level Bearer uses `{{token}}`).\n\n**Where does the handoff token come from?**\nThe Embassy backend builds a `POST /api/sso/fms-handoff` endpoint that mints a short-lived RS256 JWT signed with Embassy's private key. The mobile client calls that Embassy endpoint, receives `{ handoff_token }`, then forwards it to FMS below.\n\n**Requirements:**\n- FMS server has `EMBASSY_SSO_ENABLED=true` and the Embassy public key in place.\n- The `email` claim in the token must match a user in the FMS `users` table.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Exchange handoff for FMS token",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"handoff_token\": \"{{handoff_token}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/sso/embassy",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "sso", "embassy"]
            },
            "description": "Exchange a handoff token (from Embassy OR from the dev-mint endpoint above) for an FMS access token.\n\nFMS verifies:\n- Signature (using Embassy public key)\n- Issuer (`embassy`), audience (`fms`)\n- Expiry\n- Replay (jti not reused)\n- User exists in FMS DB (lookup by email)\n\nResponse (success):\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"token\": \"eyJhbGc...\",       // FMS access token (12h)\n    \"user\": { \"id\": 42, \"email\": \"...\", \"role\": \"...\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nResponse (user not in FMS):\n```json\n{ \"status\": false, \"msg\": \"User is not provisioned in FMS. Please contact your administrator.\" }\n```\n\nThe `token` is auto-saved to `{{token}}` — every other request in this collection now authenticates with it."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Auto-save FMS access token to collection variable",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.status && json.data && json.data.token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.data.token);",
                  "    console.log('✓ FMS access token saved to {{token}}');",
                  "  }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify auth via /api/demo",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/demo",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "demo"]
            },
            "description": "Confirms the FMS access token works. Returns the authenticated user and server time.\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": true,\n  \"msg\": \"Embassy SSO round-trip successful. You are authenticated as this FMS user:\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"authenticated_as\": { \"id\": 42, \"email\": \"...\", \"role\": \"...\", \"tenant_id\": 5 },\n    \"server_time\": \"...\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf you get 401 here, the exchange step either failed or the saved token expired (12h)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
